 "rules": [
  {
   "section": "Design rules 2.6",
   "text": "**One primary button per context.** Other actions use the button roles in §9.1: secondary → quiet (and destructive where something is removed or closed for good)."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.1",
   "text": "**Primary** — Solid brand blue, white label: The one action that moves the flow forward. One per screen or sheet."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.1",
   "text": "**One height per group** — differ by style, not size (Apple HIG). Full-width action buttons in a pinned bar, sheet or form: **56px, 18 semibold**, whatever their role. Compact inline buttons (e.g. \"View Rx\" in a content row): **48px, 16 semibold**."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.1",
   "text": "**Labels:** verb first, sentence case, no full stop, never \"Click\" / \"Tap\"."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.1",
   "text": "**States:** pressed; disabled (design-system disabled style, exempt from contrast); busy (L2). Busy spinner → label gap is 8 on every busy button. A quiet action in progress shows text only (\"Ending…\"), no spinner. **Busy labels always end with \"…\"** (\"Verifying…\", \"Sending OTP…\") (D-54)."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules L2",
   "text": "L2 — Loading primary buttons: brand-blue fill, white label, white spinner, on every screen (sign-in \"Sending OTP\", OTP \"Verifying\", any future loading primary)."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 8.6",
   "text": "**Tap targets:** **48px minimum** for everything tappable that is not a link inside a sentence: icon buttons (✕, ?, Back, zoom), buttons, chips, rows, toggles, standalone links. Enlarge the hit area, not the text. Meets Android (48dp) and iOS (44pt); WCAG 2.5.8's floor is 24px. Links inside a sentence follow WCAG 2.5.8's inline exception."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.1",
   "text": "**Button icon size steps with the button size** (D-81 F27): **56px action buttons (18px label) → 20px icon; 48px compact buttons (16px label) → 16px icon.** Icons stay on the icon scale (16 / 20 / 24) — like type and spacing, each size is a step on a fixed scale, never an in-between value; the icon is one step at or just above its label (as in Carbon, Atlassian and Fluent). **Icon-only buttons** (Back, Help, notifications, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) are not labelled buttons and keep a **20px** icon. Set centrally in by button size (`.tm-btn--lg` → 20, compact → 16, `.tm-btn--icon` → 20), overriding any size in the markup; screens never size button icons. SALT's code copy states no per-button icon size; this is a Truemeds addition."
  }
 ],
